            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Significance for Islam</strong><br>\nIn Islam, Jerusalem is considered the third holiest city after Mecca and Medina. The Dome of the Rock and Al-Aqsa Mosque on the Temple Mount are significant Islamic sanctuaries. According to Islamic tradition, the Prophet Mohammed traveled in one night from Mecca to Jerusalem and ascended to heaven from there.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Political Conflicts</strong><br>\nThe various religious claims to the city have led to conflicts over the centuries. The political situation is complex, with Israel and Palestine both laying claim to the city. Conflicts over the status of Jerusalem are often intertwined with religious tensions and have led to violence many times.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Architecture and Culture</strong><br>\nJerusalem has unique architecture and culture, strongly influenced by the three predominant religions. The city offers a mix of ancient buildings, religious sites, and modern architecture. Through the centuries, various cultures and civilizations have left their marks on the architecture and culture of the city.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
