          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Economy and Tourism</strong><br>\nTourism is an important source of income for Jerusalem, as the city attracts millions of pilgrims and tourists every year. Visitors come to see the holy sites and to experience the rich history and culture of the city. The local economy also benefits from visitors, and there are many shops and markets selling traditional goods and souvenirs.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Research</strong><br>\nThere are many educational and research institutions in Jerusalem. The Hebrew University of Jerusalem is one of the leading universities in the country and offers a wide range of study opportunities. There are also many research institutes that deal with the rich history and religious traditions of the city.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Future of Jerusalem</strong><br>\nThe future of Jerusalem is uncertain as political and religious tensions continue to exist. There is hope for peace and a mutual solution for all parties involved, but the complex challenges require patience and understanding from all sides. The city will continue to be a place of great religious and historical significance that attracts people from around the world.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
